# sui-dev-environment

Complete guide for setting up a Sui developer environment from scratch. Covers the full path from zero to a deployed package with a connected frontend.

## What this skill covers

| Section | Topics |
|---|---|
| System requirements | Linux (Ubuntu 22.04+), macOS (Monterey+), Windows (10/11) |
| Installing Sui | `suiup` (recommended), Homebrew, Chocolatey, verification, command reference table (`install`, `update`, `switch`, `show`, `self update`) |
| Configuring the Sui client | First-time setup, `client.yaml`, managing environments and addresses, key storage (`sui.keystore`), recovery phrases |
| Getting SUI tokens | Web faucet, Discord, community faucets, rate limits, balance verification |
| Creating a Move project | `sui move new`, current `Move.toml` format (automatic Sui dependency, no `[addresses]`), `Published.toml`, `Move.lock`, MVR dependencies, starter projects |
| IDE and editor setup | Move Analyzer via `suiup`, Prettier plugin, VS Code, IntelliJ, Emacs, Vim, Zed, web IDEs |
| Building and testing | `sui move build`, `#[test]` attributes, `test_scenario`, `unit_test`, `test_utils`, `debug`, coverage, Move Trace Debugger, `sui replay` |
| Publishing a package | Pre-publish checklist, `sui client publish`, package ID and UpgradeCap output, `Published.toml`, multi-network publishing, `--serialize-output` for multisig |
| Setting up a frontend | `@mysten/dapp-kit`, `@mysten/sui`, `@tanstack/react-query`, `npm create @mysten/dapp`, wallet connection, transaction signing |
| Running a local network | `sui start --with-faucet --force-regenesis`, local faucet endpoints, switching to Localnet |
| Version management | `suiup update` + `suiup switch` two-step process, version mismatch symptoms, `client/server api version mismatch` warning, installing additional tools |
| Explorers and data tools | SuiVision, Suiscan, GraphQL RPC, `sui replay` |
| Dry runs and transaction debugging | `devInspectTransactionBlock`, `--dry-run` flag, common failure causes, wallet dry run behavior |
| Best practices | Equivocation warning, collection sizing (1,000 items for vectors), 256 KB object limit, `public(package)` visibility, struct upgrade constraints, gas coin selection |

## Sources

All content is sourced exclusively from:

- [docs.sui.io](https://docs.sui.io)
- [move-book.com](https://move-book.com)

## When to use this skill

Use this skill whenever the user:

- Needs to install Sui or update to a newer version
- Is configuring the Sui CLI, managing environments, or switching networks
- Is creating a new Move project or troubleshooting `Move.toml` issues
- Needs to set up an IDE or editor for Move development
- Is writing, running, or debugging Move tests
- Is publishing a package for the first time or to a different network
- Needs to set up a React frontend with Sui dApp Kit
- Is setting up Localnet for offline development
- Hits version mismatches, dependency errors, or build failures
- Asks about `suiup`, faucets, explorers, dry runs, or gas budgets

